#
# winoracle (WARP) output above, x64; x86 identical except "ptr=4".
# Vitreo 2026-09-28 build differs on three lines:
#   WDS dynamic tex: dispatch 1 (tex 5): ... tex=6   <- WRONG: Unmap of a
#       WRITE_DISCARD dynamic texture overwrites the texture a dispatch
#       recorded earlier still reads (no rename).
#   UPD default SRV: after box update [8,12)=77 ... src=9  <- WRONG: buffer
#       UpdateSubresource with a box is dropped.
#   DNW texture: first Map(DO_NOT_WAIT) 0x00000000 <- the GPU->staging texture
#       copy is a synchronous readback inside CopyResource, so DO_NOT_WAIT can
#       never report WAS_STILL_DRAWING (correct data; the CPU stalls in the copy).
# Everything else matches: dynamic CB / buffer-SRV DISCARD rename, VB|SRV
# NO_OVERWRITE, UpdateSubresource/CopySubresourceRegion ordering on buffers,
# buffer Map(DO_NOT_WAIT) -> DXGI_ERROR_WAS_STILL_DRAWING.
